<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Every user-facing string of the slot lives here, and the matching tree lives in values-ru/.
    Nothing in this app compiles prose into Kotlin: a literal in a `Text(...)` or in a
    `contentDescription` is a string no translator can reach and no pseudolocale can stretch
    (`scripts/core/localization.mjs`, `locale.hardcoded`).

    `about_privacy_url` is deliberately translatable="false": a policy address is not copy, and the
    default configuration is the only source of truth for it. A copy of it under values-ru/ would be
    a second source for one URL, which is the drift `documents/slot-...` records.

    Every `%1$s` / `%1$d` here is matched position for position in values-ru/ — a dropped or
    renumbered argument is what `localeProblems()` (scripts/core/policy.mjs) fails the pack for.
-->
